.TH SDL_DEFINE_PIXELFOURCC 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_DEFINE_PIXELFOURCC \- A macro for defining custom FourCC pixel formats.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_pixels.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_DEFINE_PIXELFOURCC(A, B, C, D) SDL_FOURCC(A, B, C, D)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
For example, defining
.BR SDL_PIXELFORMAT_YV12
looks like this:

.IP
.EX
SDL_DEFINE_PIXELFOURCC('Y', 'V', '1', '2')
.EE
.PP

.SH MACRO PARAMETERS
.TP
.I A
the first character of the FourCC code\[char46]
.TP
.I B
the second character of the FourCC code\[char46]
.TP
.I C
the third character of the FourCC code\[char46]
.TP
.I D
the fourth character of the FourCC code\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a format value in the style of
.BR SDL_PixelFormat \[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this macro from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

